-- fooddb.lua -- what each food DOES, GENERATED by tools/gen_fooddb.py from
-- the CatsEyeXI server's own item scripts (github.com/CatsAndBoats/catseyexi,
-- branch `stable`). Do not hand-edit; rebuild with:
--   python tools/gen_fooddb.py     (maintainer only, ships with updates)
--
-- WHY THIS EXISTS: FFXI's food status icon is generic -- it never says WHICH
-- food is up, so after a relog the game cannot tell you what you are getting.
-- feature/foodwatch knows what you ate; this table is what lets it say what
-- that food does.
--
-- DISPLAY ONLY, and the split is load-bearing: this table must NEVER be used
-- to decide whether an item IS food. That answer stays learned from the FOOD
-- effect moving (feature/foodwatch), so a food the server adds tomorrow is
-- still remembered and still eatable -- it just has no stats to hover. Wire
-- this into detection and the "dlac ships no food list" guarantee is gone and
-- a stale copy starts deciding what counts as food.
--
-- Text is the server script's OWN English header, verbatim -- not a
-- translation of its addMod calls (86 mod names, every one a chance to
-- mislabel a stat the player cannot check). Phrasing is therefore
-- inconsistent between foods: different contributors wrote those comments.
--
--   d = duration in seconds   s = the effect lines, in server order
--
-- Loaded lazily and fails soft (feature/foodwatch.statsFor) -- a missing or
-- partial table drops the tooltip back to the client's own item
-- Description, never errors.
